Package: FMR
Title: Functional Mendelian Randomization with a Functional Instrument
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Chi-Shian", "Dai", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "cdai@gs.ncku.edu.tw",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-9711-6295")),
    person("Cai", "Li", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the causal effect of an exposure on an outcome when the instrument
    is a function, such as the genotype of the variants of a gene indexed by genomic
    position, and allows a direct (pleiotropic) effect of the instrument on the outcome.
    The instrument enters through its functional principal component scores, the direct
    effect is a penalized B-spline with the penalty chosen by generalized cross-validation,
    and inference uses a bootstrap-t interval studentized by the sandwich standard error.
    Also provides the test of no direct effect and the paper's simulation design.
